<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<usx version="3.0">
  <book code="JAS" style="id">OZHEM - ELOYI TRANSLATION PROJECT</book>
  <para style="h">Ozhemisi</para>
  <para style="toc1">Kwupu Mbaa Ozhemisi</para>
  <para style="toc2">Ozhemisi</para>
  <para style="toc3">Ozhm</para>
  <para style="mt2">Kwupu Mbaa</para>
  <para style="mt1">OZHEMISI</para>
  <para style="imt">Kambu Iyemo</para>
  <para style="ip">Kwupu kwɔlɛ, Ozhemisi umanyiwu Ɔzhizɔsi gba a ka ngwu le. Ozhemisi ele uwu gba akwu u to keyi uwu ɔshɔshi uwu Ɔzhɛrusalɛ le. A ka kwupu kwɔlɛ &lt;&lt;laa enzu umba Ukpo lɛɛbi umba bɔkɔ o kpashaa munamuna mu kwudu kwɔlɛ awu.&gt;&gt; Ozhemisi e wo ɛduma mu aba gba a ta enzu okpa le mekeka iyi ilukwu mbala luzɛ undu Umbwalu mu kwudu kwɔlɛ. E so iso mu meka iyi apula gyɔɔ kyamate kiya ingyi kwuwo mbala rewa, ipwama, luzɛ undu esheshi, imamate, ikwidufulo mbala ɛduma iwomo, iso isomo mu kenzu ungepo, ilukwu, itumo, ɛnwu ikwumo mbala igyi ɛnwu ma, ombwu izɔma uwu enzu, iso iyɛku isomo laa ɛnwu ikwumo, idiyimo mbala Ukpo ilɛma.</para>
  <para style="ip">Kwupu kwɔlɛ kwu siso iyɛkɔkɔ tee ɛduma iwomo mbala ikwidufulo i zɛ kyaa mu Okrasi imbwaluma.</para>
  <para style="iot">Iso Iyi I Yi Memi</para>
  <para style="io1">Kambu Iyemo (1.1)</para>
  <para style="io1">Ikwidufulo mbala Ilukwu (1.2-8)</para>
  <para style="io1">Rewa mbala Kiya ingyi kwuwo (1.9-11)</para>
  <para style="io1">Ipwama (1.12-18)</para>
  <para style="io1">Iso ipwama mbala iwomo (1.19-27)</para>
  <para style="io1">Iyemalu mɛka iyi kwusɛ isɛma (2.1-13)</para>
  <para style="io1">Ikwidufulo mbala ɛduma iwomo (2.14-26)</para>
  <para style="io1">Umbwalu mbala ɔtinɛ wu (3.1-18)</para>
  <para style="io1">Umbwalu mbala kwudu kwɔlɛ (4.1—5.6)</para>
  <para style="io1">Okpa ikikɔ ikikɔ (5.7-20)</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="JAS 1" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JAS 1:1" />Kwupu kwɔlɛ kwu ngyi mbaa mi, Imi Ozhemisi, Umɛgba uwu Ukpo mbala uwu Ɔkwu Ɔzhizɔsi Okrasi:</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JAS 1:1">mi gbɛlɛ yi ɛnyi lɛɛbi lunyi enzu umba Ukpo umba bɔkɔ o kpashaa munamuna mu kwudu kwɔlɛ awu.<verse eid="JAS 1:1" /></para>
  <para style="s">Ikwidufulo Mbala Ilukwu</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="JAS 1:2" />Ɛmɛnɛ mi, kwuyengwunanguna bɔkɔ inyashi i du yi, la kwa yi kiya ingyi ɔnyɛ, <verse eid="JAS 1:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JAS 1:3" />moo lu yitu te ipwama iyi ikwu idu lu fulo yi mu Ɔzhizɔsi, i kyo yi idu iyimo mo. <verse eid="JAS 1:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JAS 1:4" />La lu vɔngɔ idu iyimo mu iyinayina akwɛyi lu kɔma, luu kwu enzu umba bɔkɔ ɔ nyɔlɔma mu kiya ingyinangyina. <verse eid="JAS 1:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JAS 1:5" />Onzu uwu bɔkɔ e yi ilukwu mo, ba la nda Ukpo uwu bɔkɔ ee shi mu egbo ikpɛnyi ba a za anu mo awu. <verse eid="JAS 1:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JAS 1:6" />Kwuye ungwu onzu ba a nda kwoya te lo shi wu ilukwu, le fulo eyi, le yi egbo epepo mo. Mo onzu uwu egbo epo e yi kyamate agba iyi embyi tayi, iyi bɔkɔ kwokpo kwu fya yi i re te, i gba te awu. <verse eid="JAS 1:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JAS 1:7" />Onzu awu tayi, le fulo eyi te a fya kiya kinyinyi mbaa Ukpo mo. <verse eid="JAS 1:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JAS 1:8" />Onzu awu tayi ɔ wɛlɛ ma wu mo, kwuwongu a ŋanga egbo wu mo kwuyengwunanguna bi.<verse eid="JAS 1:8" /></para>
  <para style="s">Rewa Mbala Kiya Ingyi Kwuwo</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="JAS 1:9" />Umɛnɛ ɔyirewa, la mu ɔnyɛ te Ukpo ee kyo wu mo. <verse eid="JAS 1:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JAS 1:10" />Umɛnɛ uwu e yi kwuwo ba la mwɔnyɛ te Ukpo a zɔ wu inyɛma wu, mo u wu mbala kiya ingyi kwuwo wu o kpɛdɔma ndii mutu uwɔniyi kyamate edodo tayi. <verse eid="JAS 1:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JAS 1:11" />Mo gba ɔnu u kwo mu ilama, uzu wu u ngbɛ edodo ma akwɛyi i fumo mɛzhi akwɛyi woshi yi u tomo ndii. Tatayi gba onzu uwu e yi kwuwo e yi le. Ee yi mu igɔma iyawu la ɛduma wu iwomo akwɛyi mutu uwɔniyi ɔ pwa te e yi fo.<verse eid="JAS 1:11" /></para>
  <para style="s">Inyashi Mbala Ipwama</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="JAS 1:12" />Onzu uwu bɔkɔ ɔ pwa wu ma ba a tama mo, e yi ɔnyɛ uwakwu, mo mizhikembo yi, a na rigbɛ ingyi kwunyɔ ungwɔkpɔ ba ɔkpɔɔ ungwu bɔkɔ Ukpo e so e shi mɛzhi te e shi enzu umba bɔkɔ o kpo lukwu wu.<verse eid="JAS 1:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="JAS 1:13" />Onzu uwu o pwa wu ma laa zɔ te, &lt;&lt;Ukpo gba e ye mi mu ipwama le.&gt;&gt; Mo Ukpo, o pwa wu ma mo, u wu ba a pwa onzu uwunawuna ma mo. <verse eid="JAS 1:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JAS 1:14" />Ekweyi iyi onzu gba i kyoro wu mo akwɛyi i ka wu la ipwama le. <verse eid="JAS 1:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JAS 1:15" />Mizhikembo iyi ekweyi i shi rifo, akwɛyi i mba ingbomo, gba ingbomo i bulɔma-a, i bo la lukwu.<verse eid="JAS 1:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="JAS 1:16" />Ɛmɛnɛ mi umbafyafyimi, onzu uwunawuna le kyoro yi mo mo. <verse eid="JAS 1:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JAS 1:17" />Rɛshi ingyi kiya ingyesheshi ingyinangyina ki ngyi moshi mbaa Edego-ala uwu bɔkɔ e wo ɔnu mbala ɔvya mbala elovyo iyi bɔkɔ i lemo moshi awu, uwu bɔkɔ e turumo kyamate kwundu ungwu ɔnu na ungwu uwɛyi na ungwu onzu mo awu. <verse eid="JAS 1:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JAS 1:18" />A ka nzu la ongbulolo uwu iso, ki na yi ma akwɛyi ki fya kwunyɔ ungwepo kaa la ki kwu umba kwonze mu apula lɛɛbi iyi bɔkɔ e wo.<verse eid="JAS 1:18" /></para>
  <para style="s">Iso Ipwama Mbala Iwomo.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="JAS 1:19" />Ɛmɛnɛ mi, onzonzu la ngbɛndu mu iso ɛlɛ: Uwewe le wo kwupapa ungwu iso ipwama, tetete uwu ba la gba opwu efyefya mo, ba lakwu u wo amba efyefya mo. <verse eid="JAS 1:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JAS 1:20" />Mi so ɛlɛ kwuwongu bɔkɔ amba umba onzu ɔ bo la kiya ingyeshi ingyi Ukpo a gyi mo. <verse eid="JAS 1:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JAS 1:21" />Kwuwo ngwɔlɛ la lu lafya la ira iyinayina iwomo kaa lu mbwalu iso iyi Ukpo iyi bɔkɔ o so yi mu egbo yi awu, moo inyi gba i sa yi ma le.<verse eid="JAS 1:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="JAS 1:22" />La lu kwu wangbalu mu iso iyi Ukpo byi mo. Onzu uwu e wo ɛlɛ ba e kyoro ɛnwu ma. La lu wo kiya ingyi iso iyi Ukpo i zɔ te lo wo. <verse eid="JAS 1:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JAS 1:23" />Onzu uwunawuna uwu bɔkɔ a pwa iso iyi Ukpo byi ba e wo kiya ingyi i zɔ te lo wo mo, e yi kyamate onzu uwu bɔkɔ e yese ɛnwu mu umɛbɛ tayi, <verse eid="JAS 1:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JAS 1:24" />akwɛyi a gba a kama. I to Kwuye gyɔɔ mo akwɛyi a ka la kuleyi iyi bɔkɔ uwu e yi. <verse eid="JAS 1:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="JAS 1:25" />Onzu uwu ba aa bɔ eyi mu ɛrama iyi Ukpo iyɔkpɔɔ, iyi bɔkɔ i sa nzu ma le, akwɛyi a mbwalu yi iyɔkpɔɔ, Ukpo e shi wu esheshi wu kwuwongu iwomo wu ɛlɛ.<verse eid="JAS 1:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="JAS 1:26" />Onzu uwunawuna uwu e to ɛnwu te uwu akwu u mbwalu Ukpo, uwu ba e yi kenzu wu mo mo, e kyoro ɛnwu ma byi, Ukpo imbwaluma wu ba akwiyi umbwa. <verse eid="JAS 1:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="JAS 1:27" />Luzɛ undu bɔkɔ Ukpo Edego-ala a gyi, undu bɔkɔ lu wuluma gba akwu te, lo yese mba ɛmɛ umbese mbala eko wakpanuma kwuyengwu o yi mu inyashi mbala izɛ gboo mba inzumbira iyi kwudu kwɔlɛ.<verse eid="JAS 1:27" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JAS 1" />
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="JAS 2" />
  <para style="s1">La lu Zɔ Kwusɛ Mo</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JAS 2:1" />Ɛmɛnɛ mi, lunyi umba bɔkɔ lu kwidu lu fulo mu Ɔkwu nzu Ɔzhizɔsi Okrasi uwu inzumbɛku awu, la lu zɔ kusɛ mo. <verse eid="JAS 2:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JAS 2:2" />Akwiyi gba enzu wepo o bo mbaa ɛlu ikpalama yi, akwɛyi ukpɛnyi mba e lo karika unga egolu mbala ekpayi iyi abwa, akwɛyi uwufo ba akwu ɔyirewa uwu bɔkɔ e lo ashɔgiri e kyo e fyemo tete. <verse eid="JAS 2:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JAS 2:3" />Akwɛyi lu yese mbaa onzu uwu bɔkɔ e lo ekpayi iyi abwa awu akwɛyi lu za wu te, &lt;&lt;Bo kaa ŋɔ mu kagyi ungeshi kɛlɛ te, &lt;&lt;Ɔyirewa awu ba lu za wu te, &lt;&lt;Uŋɔ ri tayi&gt;&gt; mo de ba &lt;&lt;Ŋɔma mɛzhi mbaa alɛ mi te,&gt;&gt; <verse eid="JAS 2:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JAS 2:4" />Gba lu wo tayi, lu zɔ kusɛ meka yi akwɛyi lu zɔ ombu la egbo iyira.<verse eid="JAS 2:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="JAS 2:5" />La lu ngbɛ kwɔlu kaa la lu pwa ɛmɛnɛ mi, Ukpo a ŋa ayirewa umba kwudu kwɔlɛ kaa lo kwu enzu umbakwu kwuwongu o mbwalu Ɔzhizɔsi kaa lo ri ogu uwu ɛzhi iyi bɔkɔ e so te e shi umba bɔkɔ o pwu idɛnyi wu mo? <verse eid="JAS 2:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JAS 2:6" />Lunyi ba lu kpo ayirewa eseye. Akwu enzu umbakwu mbɔlɛ gba o kpa yi ata le mo re? Akwu umba gba o pyipyi yi o ka mbaa ombu le mo re? <verse eid="JAS 2:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JAS 2:7" />Akwu umba gba o so iyira iyi Ɔzhizɔsi uwayi awu le mo re?<verse eid="JAS 2:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="JAS 2:8" />Akwiyi gba lu mbwalu ɛrama iyi Ada Ɔsu Ukpo iyi bɔkɔ o ka mu kwokpo ungwu Ukpo te, &lt;&lt;Pwidɛnyi iyi onzu unɔ kpaŋa kyamate ɛnwu ŋɔ te.&gt;&gt; Gba lu wo tayi de ba lu wo ɔnyɛ. <verse eid="JAS 2:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JAS 2:9" />Akwiyi gba lu zɔ kusɛ, de ba lu ngbomo-o, Ukpo ba e yi yi ombu kwuwongu lu fo ɛrama wu ma. <verse eid="JAS 2:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JAS 2:10" />Gba onzu a mbwalu ɛrama iyi Ukpo lɛɛbi ba e fo ikpɛnyi ma, i zɔ te e fo yi mo lɛɛbi ma. <verse eid="JAS 2:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JAS 2:11" />Mo Ukpo uwu bɔkɔ a zɔ te &lt;&lt;Lo to kaya mo le&gt;&gt; uwu gba a zɔ te &lt;&lt;Lo ngbɛ onzu mo tete le.&gt;&gt; Gba ŋɔ to kaya mo ba ŋɔ ngbɛ onzu, de ba ŋɔ kwu u fo ɛrama ma mo.<verse eid="JAS 2:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="JAS 2:12" />Iso isomo mbala iwomo yi li yi mate enzu umba bɔkɔ Ukpa a ba zɔ mba ombwu mu ɛrama iyi i wanzu ma tayi. <verse eid="JAS 2:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JAS 2:13" />Ɔnu uwu ombu izɔma, Ukpo a ma eyembembyi iyi onzu uwu bɔkɔ a ma eyembembyi iyi enzu, moo eyembembyi i ka ombwu mo.<verse eid="JAS 2:13" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ikwidufulo Mbala Ɛduma</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="JAS 2:14" />Ɛmɛnɛ mi akwiyi gba onzu a zɔ te e yi ikwu idu lu fulo ba e yi ɛduma iyeshi mo, esheshi yi ba akwu mbɛ? Ikwidufulo wu ɛnyi i do wu isama? <verse eid="JAS 2:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JAS 2:15" />Akwiyi gba ugɔ uwu okpayi mbala uwu kiya ingyirimo a kpa <note caller="+" style="f" />umɛnɛ ɔnzɔnu naa okokpayi ma, <verse eid="JAS 2:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JAS 2:16" />akwɛyi onzu uwufo a za wu te, &lt;&lt;So moloto Ukpo le shi ŋɔ ekpayi mbala kiya ingyirimo ingyi bɔkɔ ŋɔ gyi awu,&gt;&gt; ba e wo kinyinyi kaa la sa wu ugɔ awu ma mo, a mbwa wu ma mungye? <verse eid="JAS 2:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JAS 2:17" />Tegba ikwu idu lu fulo i yi le, akwiyi gba i kyo mbala ɛduma mo i yi kyamate ukpɛzhi uwu onzu tayi.<verse eid="JAS 2:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="JAS 2:18" />Onzu uwufo ba aa zɔ te, &lt;&lt;Uŋɔ ŋɔ yi ikwu idu lu fulo imi ba mi yi ɛduma.&gt;&gt;</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JAS 2:18">Zɔ mi ɛduma ŋa iyi bɔkɔ i kyo mbala ikwu idu lu fulo mo akwɛyi imi ba mi zɔ ŋɔ ɛduma mi iyi mi wo mbala ikwu idu lu fulo mi. <verse eid="JAS 2:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JAS 2:19" />Ŋɔ nyama te Ukpo akwu ukpɛnyi? Ee te gba i yi le! Eyo umbeyi lala o nyama tete ba o pulama kwuwongu o wiyi.<verse eid="JAS 2:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="JAS 2:20" />Uŋɔ orondo ele, o zɔ ŋɔ dɛ gba ŋɔ yitu te ikwu idu lu fulo iyi bɔkɔ iyi ɛduma mo akwu shaa bi le? <verse eid="JAS 2:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JAS 2:21" />Usɔkwu nzu Aburamu kɔ, o ma ototo wu kwuwongu ɛduma iyi bɔkɔ e wo bɔkɔ a ra la umɛ wu Aziki e shi rɛshi mu kwumbwu ungwu isabɔ awu mo re? <verse eid="JAS 2:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JAS 2:22" />Ŋɔ ma, ikwu idu fulo wu mbala ɛduma wu bɔkɔ i zɛ kya, akwɛyi ikwu idu fulo wu ba i nyɔlɔma kwuwongu ɛduma iyi bɔkɔ e wo. <verse eid="JAS 2:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JAS 2:23" />Kwokpo ungwu Ukpo ba kwu nyɔlɔ ma bɔkɔ kwu zɔ te, &lt;&lt;Aburamu e kwidu e fulo mu Ukpo, akwɛyi Ukpo ba a wa wu te akwu onzu uwu ototo,&gt;&gt; akwɛyi Ukpo a ya wu te, &lt;&lt;Umɛza mi&gt;&gt;. <verse eid="JAS 2:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JAS 2:24" />Kekelele i zɔ te, onzu akwu ototo kwuwongu ikwu idu fulo kɛɛkyi mo, i kyo ɛduma tete. <verse eid="JAS 2:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="JAS 2:25" />Tatayi gba i yi le, Orahabu u to kaya awu o ya wu te onzu ototo kwuwongu ɛduma iyi bɔkɔ e wo bɔkɔ e shi riyi oga la enzu umba Izirɛ bɔkɔ o wɔ o bo o ŋanda kizɛ awu ma akwɛyi ba e shi mbo o kama mu ɔgwuzɛ owa awu. <verse eid="JAS 2:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="JAS 2:26" />Kyamate ɛnwu iyi bɔkɔ i yi kwundu mo akwu ukpɛzhi uwu kiya awu, tatayi gba ikwu idu fulo iyi bɔkɔ iyi ɛduma mo i yi le.<verse eid="JAS 2:26" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JAS 2" />
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="JAS 3" />
  <para style="s1">Wambwalu Lo Gbo Ɔtinɛ Mba Mo</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JAS 3:1" />Ɛmɛnɛ mi, akwu kpɛkpɛyi gba la lu kwu wa zɔ ɛzu le mo, kwuwongu lu yitu te, Ukpo e yo nzu kinzu wa zɔ ɛzu kwuyo a ka uwewe ma. <verse eid="JAS 3:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JAS 3:2" />Kinzu ki lɛfyi kwuyengwunanguna, gba onzu e ngbomo mu iso wu isomo mo, onzu awu a gyirima munamuna, onzu awu tayi e do ɛnwu irima gbagiri.<verse eid="JAS 3:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="JAS 3:3" />Gba ki lo uri mu kenzu unga Onya kaa le wo iyi bɔkɔ ki gyi, ki do te ki re la onya ngyɔɔ mbaa bɔkɔ ki gyi, <verse eid="JAS 3:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JAS 3:4" />naa egbo nzu li so mbaa kwoda ungwu embyi ungwɔkwu. La imbwulama ngwu ba ombirigizhi gba a pyangu le, tetete, kwɔsɔ ungwɛri te gba u pɛ kwɔda a ra ngwu akwɛyi pyangu e re ngwu mbaa bɔkɔ a gyi le. <verse eid="JAS 3:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JAS 3:5" />Tete ɔtinɛ akwu kiya ingyɛri mu ɛnwu iyi onzu ba a bɔma gyɔɔ te e do kiya ingyɛkwu iwomo. La lu gba la lu ngbɛndu te ɔyi ɔkɛkyi u do kwokata ungwɔkwu ipumo. <verse eid="JAS 3:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JAS 3:6" />Ɔtinɛ uwu onzu e yi kyamate ɔyi tayi, meka iyi ɛnwu iyi onzu uwu gba a ka ira le. Ɔtinɛ e tutu ɛnwu iyi onzu kpɛkpɛyi ma, a ngbɛ kwunyɔ wu ɛdɔma, kyamate ɔyi uwu aleku u yi ma wu tayi. <verse eid="JAS 3:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JAS 3:7" />Izɔfyi umbanambana laa afyi umboshi laa umba bɔkɔ o zɛ mu ibu mbo laa umba bɔkɔ o yi membyi, kpɛkpɛmba o gwu mbo mo, akwɛyi enzu ba o gwu mbo mo. <verse eid="JAS 3:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JAS 3:8" />Onzu uwu bɔkɔ e domo te e gwu ɔtinɛ ma ba e yi mo. Ɔtinɛ e yi ɛtu kyamate ɛtu iyi ɔgbazhi tayi.<verse eid="JAS 3:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="JAS 3:9" />Mu ɔtinɛ nzu ele gba ki gbo Ɔkwu nzu, Ete nzu ɔya le, tete akwu mu ɔtinɛ ele gba ki siso iyira iyi enzu umba bɔkɔ Ukpo e wo mbo o wɔ wu le. <verse eid="JAS 3:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JAS 3:10" />Mu kenzu kɛlɛ tete gba ki so iso iyeshi mbala iyira iyi enzu le. Ɛmɛnɛ mi ishoshi te lakwu tayi mo. <verse eid="JAS 3:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JAS 3:11" />Kwubu kwu tembyi umbeshi mbala umbira kwuye kwukpɛnyi mo. <verse eid="JAS 3:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JAS 3:12" />Ɛmɛnɛ mi, uwɛyi uwu oboriyo u do te u wa la imuma iyi olifu? Nana uwɛyi uwu oremi u wala imuma iyi uwɛyi uwu oboriyo? Tatayi kwubu kwukpɛnyi kwu tembyi umba otopwa mbala umbeshi kwuye kwukpɛnyi mo.<verse eid="JAS 3:12" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ilukwu Iyi I Ingyi Moshi</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="JAS 3:13" />Uwe meka yi bɔkɔ e yi amasa mbala ilukwu? Onzu awu la zɔ yi mu luzɛ wu undeshi izɛma, le wo ɛduma la egbo mɛzhi mbala amasa. <verse eid="JAS 3:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JAS 3:14" />Gba lunyi o yi rise ingyɛkwu mbala imɛyɛyi mu egbo yi, la lu kwu ɛnwu te lu kwu enzu umba ilukwu mo, moo ɛlɛ akwu imulo. <verse eid="JAS 3:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JAS 3:15" />Ilukwu ɛlɛ te i ngyi moshi mbaa Ukpo mo, i wɔ mu kwudu kwɔlɛ, mbaa enzu umba bɔkɔ o yi kwundu ɔpɛriri mamba mo, i wɔ mbaa onzu uwoyi. <verse eid="JAS 3:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JAS 3:16" />Moo munamuna mbaa bɔkɔ enzu o wo rise ingyi esu mbala imɛmɛmba, mɔmɔ gba ŋɔ du ovyo mbala ira iyinayina le.<verse eid="JAS 3:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="JAS 3:17" />Ilukwu iyi bɔkɔ i wɔ moshi i ka pɛriri le; i bo la ovyo mo; i wo wɔnu mbala enzu mo; i lomo la enzu; i ma eyembembyi iyi enzu mbala ɛduma iwomo iyesheshi; i zɔ kusɛ mo ba i mwangba mo. <verse eid="JAS 3:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JAS 3:18" />Enzu wa gyi iŋɔma iyi oloto o somo iyi oloto, ba o fya iyeshi.<verse eid="JAS 3:18" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JAS 3" />
  <chapter number="4" style="c" sid="JAS 4" />
  <para style="s1">Imɛza Irimo Mbala Kwudu Kwɔlɛ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JAS 4:1" />Kimbe ki ta yi itumo mbala ewa? I wɔ mbaa amasa iyira iyi lu ka mu egbo yi. <verse eid="JAS 4:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JAS 4:2" />Lunyi lu gyi apula gyɔɔ ba lu fya yi ma mo akwɛyi lu ngbɛ enzu, lu gba lu wo ekweyi iyi apula iyi enzu, lunyi ba lu fya yi ma mo kwuwongu lu nda Ukpo mo. <verse eid="JAS 4:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JAS 4:3" />Kwuye ungwu lu nda Ukpo kiya lala lu fya yi ma mo, moo lu nda kwuwongu ɔnyɛ uwu ɛnwu yi kɛɛkyi, lu gyite la lu sa ugɔ uwu ɛnwu yi kɛɛkyi.<verse eid="JAS 4:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="JAS 4:4" />Lunyi enzu wa to kaya mbɔlɛ, lu yitu te imɛza irimo mbala kwudu kwɔlɛ akwu egewa mbala Ukpo mo re? Onzu uwunawuna uwu a gyi te kaa le ri imɛza mbala kwudu kwɔlɛ, e wo ɛnwu wu ogewa uwu Ukpo. <verse eid="JAS 4:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JAS 4:5" />Naa lu ma te Kwokpo ungwu Ukpo kwu so bi re te Kwundu uwu Ukpo uwu e shi nzu awu e wo rise gyɔɔ mo? <verse eid="JAS 4:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JAS 4:6" />Ukpo ba e shi nzu esheshi iyɛku kyamate bɔkɔ Kwokpo ungwu Ukpo kwu so te:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="JAS 4:6">&lt;&lt;Enzu umba bɔkɔ o fu lo ɛmba mu kadu, Ukpo a nya mba mɛzhi</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JAS 4:6">enzu umba bɔkɔ o gyi ɛnwu mba ma ba Ukpo e shi mbo esheshi.&gt;&gt;<verse eid="JAS 4:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="JAS 4:7" />Kwuwongwu ɔlɛ, ra la ɛnwu ŋɔ ka shi Ukpo. Uŋɔ ba towo ɔgwuzɛ uwu onzu uwoyi ma akwɛyi a renya e shi ŋɔ. <verse eid="JAS 4:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JAS 4:8" />La lu turu gbala Ukpo akwɛyi uwu ba e turu a gbayi lunyi enzu umba ingbomo la lu lafya la kiya ingyira iwomo, la lu nɔngɔ egbo yi ma lunyi umba egbo epo. <verse eid="JAS 4:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JAS 4:9" />La lu wo ubu ugyi, la lu wo obobyi, la lu lo oga. La lu lafya la lu ŋɔ kaa la lu lo oga, la lu lafya la ɔnyɛ imwuma kaa la lu wo ubugyi. <verse eid="JAS 4:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JAS 4:10" />La lu gyi ɛnwu yi ma mu idu iyi Ukpo akwɛyi uwu ba e fulo yi kadu.<verse eid="JAS 4:10" /></para>
  <para style="s">La lu Zɔ Esu Ombwu Mo</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="JAS 4:11" />Ɛmɛnɛ mi la lu tutu esu ma mo, gba onzu e so ungwoyi naa a zɔ ombu uwura uwu umanyi wu, ɛrama iyi Ukpo gba e so ungwoyi yi le. Gba onzu e wo tayi onzu awu akwu mbwalu ɛrama mo, akwu u tutu yi mo. <verse eid="JAS 4:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JAS 4:12" />Ukpo kɛɛkyi gba e shi ɛrama le uwu gba ba a zɔ ombu le, uwu gba e do te a sa enzu mo le naa e lo enzu inyashi le. Kwuwongwu ɔlɛ o ya ŋa te bɔkɔ uŋɔ ŋɔ zɔ ombu uwu onzu uwufo?<verse eid="JAS 4:12" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ki Kwɛnwu Iyi Kwɔnyi Kwɔlɛ Mo</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="JAS 4:13" />La lu pwa, lunyi umba bɔkɔ lu zɔ te, &lt;&lt; Ɔnɛnɛ naa kwɔnyi kwɔlɛ ki re mu kwuse kwɔlɛ naa kwɔngu, ki ŋɔ mɔmɔ kari ngyɔɔ kaa la ki wo rishi kaa la ki ri kwule,&gt;&gt; awu. <verse eid="JAS 4:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JAS 4:14" />Lunyi ba lu yitu iyi kiya ingyi ki bi wo kwɔnyi kwɔlɛ mo. Kwunyɔ yi akwu kwuwongu mbɛ? Kwu yi kyamate ebwu iyi bɔkɔ ii wɔ kwuye bwɛɛ akwɛyi i gba ii tomo ndii tayi . <verse eid="JAS 4:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JAS 4:15" />I fate la lu zɔ te, &lt;&lt;Gba Ukpo a nyama ki yi la reyi, ki wo kiya ngyɛlɛ naa ngyɛngyi.&gt;&gt; <verse eid="JAS 4:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JAS 4:16" />Lunyi ba lu kwɛnwu mu kiya ingyi bɔkɔ lu bu wo. Ɛnwu ikwumo ɛnyi tayi i sheshi mo. <verse eid="JAS 4:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JAS 4:17" />Kwuwongwu ɔlɛ, onzu uwu bɔkɔ e yitu iyi kiya ingyi bɔkɔ ki shoshi te le wo ba e wo mo, onzu awu e ngbomo.<verse eid="JAS 4:17" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JAS 4" />
  <chapter number="5" style="c" sid="JAS 5" />
  <para style="s1">O Lo Enzu Umba Bɔkɔ O Yi Kwuwo Ilutu Malu</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JAS 5:1" />Lunyi enzu umba bɔkɔ lu yi kwuwo, la lu ngbɛ alu mu iso mi, lunyi la lu lo oga gbɔrɔrɔ kwuwongu wɔnu umbu u yi mu inyɔma munyi yi. <verse eid="JAS 5:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JAS 5:2" />Kiya ingyi kwuwo yi ki kpo ɛdɔ ma, ekpayi yi ba ela e ri yi moo. <verse eid="JAS 5:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JAS 5:3" />Egolu mbala esiliva yi i kpɔ akazhi, akazhi ɛnyi i zɔ te lu ngbomo, i pwu ɛnwu yi ma kyamate ɔyi u pwu kiya tayi. Lu yi mu kiya ingyi kwuwo ɛlu ikpalama, lunyi ba lu yitu te kwudu kwɔlɛ kwu sheye mu ibomo mo. <verse eid="JAS 5:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JAS 5:4" />La lu yese! Enzu umba bɔkɔ o wo yi ɛduma mutu, ba lu shi mbo eduwo mo awu, enzu mbamba o yi mu oga ilomo oo fu yi. Oga uwu enzu mbamba ba u ka malu iyi Ukpo edego-ala. <verse eid="JAS 5:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JAS 5:5" />Kwuye ungwu bɔkɔ lu yi mu kwudu kwɔlɛ awu, lu mwɔnyɛ gyɔɔ lu kyo lu wo kiya ingyi bɔkɔ lu gyi. Lu ri kiya ingyi ɛnwu yi i gyi akwɛyi lu lo wɔkwu kyamate izɔfyi uwu bɔkɔ o ma wu ma o gbo la ingbɛma. <verse eid="JAS 5:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JAS 5:6" />Lu shi o ngbɛ enzu umba ototo ombu uwoyi akwɛyi o ngbɛ mba ma. Enzu mbɔlɛ ba o kiri yi ewa mo.<verse eid="JAS 5:6" /></para>
  <para style="s">Idu iyimo Mbala Ukpo Ilɛma</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="JAS 5:7" />Kwuwongwu ɔlɛ, ɛmɛnɛ mi la lu yidu nzhii ba kwuyengwu igbama iyi Ɔkwu nzu Ɔzhizɔsi kyamate bɔkɔ ɔnɛgba a rigbo laa ɛzhi kaa li wala ewiri kwudu akwɛyi a rigbo laa ukpo rito mbala ukpo uwu imbwama tayi.<verse eid="JAS 5:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="JAS 5:8" />Lunyi wa mbwalu tete, la lu yidu kaa lu bɔ kpɔɔ mu imbwaluma, moo igbama iyi Ɔzhizɔsi i bo kɛlɛɛ-ɛ. <verse eid="JAS 5:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JAS 5:9" />Ɛmɛnɛ mi, lunyi la lu kyɛ esu ma mo, gba lu wo tayi lu ngbomo. U zɔ ombu awu a ndafo.<verse eid="JAS 5:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="JAS 5:10" />Ɛmɛnɛ mi, la lu vɔngɔ idu iyimo mbaa anukenzu umba Ukpo. O ma inyashi, umba ba o yidu o tanu iyi Ɔkwu nzu Ɔzhizɔsii. <verse eid="JAS 5:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JAS 5:11" />Kyamate bɔkɔ lu yitu, enzu umba bɔkɔ o yi ɔnyɛ akwu enzu umba o ri enya mba nzhii o ka mu imbwama. Lu pwa eza te Ozhobu e yidu mu inyashi wu. Mizhikembo yi Ukpo a mbwa wu ma. Moo Ukpo akwu u ma inyashi mbala eyembembyi iyi enzu. <verse eid="JAS 5:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JAS 5:12" />Ɛmɛnɛ mi, iyi bɔkɔ i ka ɛlɛ ma lɛɛbi gba akwu te, la lu vungɔma la lu to la kiya mo, laa oshi laa ɛzhi laa kiya ingyinangyina mo. &lt;&lt;Ee&gt;&gt; yi lakwu ee, &lt;&lt;Ayimo&gt;&gt; yi lakwu ayimo, gba lu so lu ka ɛlɛ ma Ukpo a ngbɛ yi ombu uwoyi.<verse eid="JAS 5:12" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ukpo Ilɛma La Ikwidufulo</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="JAS 5:13" />Kwuye ungwu lu yi mu inyashi imama, la lu lɛ Ukpo kaa la mbwa yi ma. Gba lu yi mu ɔnyɛ imwuma, la lu so amwu iyi iduma la Ukpo. <verse eid="JAS 5:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JAS 5:14" />Onzu uwunawuna uwu bɔkɔ e yi okpara uwu ɛnwu mo, la ya enzu umbakɔ umba ɔshɔshi ma kaa lo lɛ Ukpo kwuwo wu akwɛyi lo la wu anyi umba ɔlifu mu reshi, kwuyengwu bɔkɔ o yi mu Ukpo ilɛma mu ɛnyi iyi Ɔkwu nzu Ɔzhizɔsi. <verse eid="JAS 5:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JAS 5:15" />Ukpo ilɛma uwu bɔkɔ o lɛ mu ikwu idu lu fulo e bo onzu awu ofya ma; Ukpo e yi wu mo. Gba e ngbo la Ukpo mo, Ukpo a gba yi a kpa wu. <verse eid="JAS 5:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JAS 5:16" />Kwuwo kwɔlɛ, la lu so ingbomo yi la esu kaa lu lɛ Ukpo kwuwongu esu kaa Ukpo le bo yi efya ma. Ukpo ilɛma iyi onzu ongbulolo i yi ekpasu. <verse eid="JAS 5:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JAS 5:17" />Anukenzu Elazha akwu onzu kyamate kinzu tete, akwɛyi a lɛ Ukpo iyɛkɔkɔ te Ukpo le tumo mo, Ukpo ba e tumo mo nzhii ba lɔri lola la evya ɛrɛnyi. <verse eid="JAS 5:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JAS 5:18" />Akwɛyi a gba a lɛ Ukpo kpɔ te Ukpo la gba la itumo ŋa akwɛyi Ukpo a gba la itumo, akwɛyi ɛzhi i wɔ la ewiri gyɔɔ.<verse eid="JAS 5:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="JAS 5:19" />Ɛmɛnɛ mi, gba onzu uwufo meka yi a lafya la ɔgwuzɛ uwu Ukpo ɔlɛ, lunyi la lu gyakpɔɔ kaa lu gba wu ma le bo mu ɔgwuzɛ. <verse eid="JAS 5:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JAS 5:20" />Lunyi la lu lolo te: Onzu uwunawuna uwu bɔkɔ a gba la onzu uwu ingbomo a ta mu ɔgwuzɛ uwu Ukpo a sa onzu awu ma mu lukwu undɔkpɔɔ. Ukpo a gba la ingbomo iyi bɔkɔ onzu awu e ngbo gyɔɔ awu a kpa wu.<verse eid="JAS 5:20" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JAS 5" />
</usx>